      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe LoRA benchmark launcher appends optional server flags without separators. Enabling two or more produces an invalid argument such as `--disable-custom-all-reduce--enable-mscclpp`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Separate the three optional flags in the constructed command.\n- Add a CPU-only regression covering all eight flag combinations.\n- Remove an existing redundant f-string prefix in the touched file so Ruff passes.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo model or inference code changes. `python -m pytest benchmark/lora/test_launch_server.py -q`: 1 passed (all eight combinations).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable; this only fixes benchmark server command construction.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] `python -m ruff check` and `python -m ruff format --check` on both changed files\n- [x] `git diff --check`\n- [x] CPU-only regression test\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #36040279500](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36040279500)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36040279064](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36040279064)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
